1. **A method of preparing a double-sided bumped semiconductor substrate, the method comprising:**

providing a semiconductor substrate having a first surface and a second surface opposite the first surface;

forming a plurality of conductive through-substrate interconnects extending between the first surface and the second surface;

forming, over the first surface, a first dielectric layer and a first redistribution structure electrically coupled to respective ones of the conductive through-substrate interconnects;

forming a plurality of first conductive bumps over the first surface, the first conductive bumps being electrically coupled to the first redistribution structure;

temporarily securing the first surface of the semiconductor substrate to a carrier such that the first conductive bumps are protected by the carrier;

while the semiconductor substrate is secured to the carrier, forming, over the second surface, a second dielectric layer and a second redistribution structure electrically coupled to respective ones of the conductive through-substrate interconnects;

forming a plurality of second conductive bumps over the second surface, the second conductive bumps being electrically coupled to the second redistribution structure; and

removing the carrier to expose the first conductive bumps, thereby producing the double-sided bumped semiconductor substrate having the first conductive bumps disposed on the first surface and the second conductive bumps disposed on the second surface.
